Z||000000||Loki||10-13-2001||10:39 PM||||  Well we had a blast, Had about 7-9 Fiero's there. Was nice to finally have faces with the names. Will post pics once I get em uploaded...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/fieroloki/loki_sig.gif">    <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/fieroloki/w4[1].gif"> <BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
Z||000001||Smoooooth GT||10-13-2001||11:12 PM||||Loki...   I wish I could have been there, I hope to see some pic's soon..  Who showed up??  talk to you later...  Steve<P>------------------<BR>NOS Injected 2.8L V/6<BR>UNDER CONSTRUCTION   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever3000||10-14-2001||02:27 AM||||There were 8 Fieros.  I'll need some help with the names, but the attendees were: John Fussell & his wife, Loki (Mike), IwannaIRM (Steve Wagner), Steve (had the black car w/3800SC), Loyde & friend, Pat (Wilson, I think), Jacob, and myself & my son Bryan.  I saw another couple whom I didn't meet, thought I'd meet them at dinner but they didn't go.  Forgive me for not remembering all the names.<P>Once again it was proven that Fiero owners are great people.  I enjoyed meeting & talking with everybody.  Looking forward to doing it again, except for being humbled by my inferior technical knowledge - let me tell you, those people know their stuff about Fieros!<P>Took 5 hours to drive up there in the rain, but it was a very smooth 4 hour drive home on dry roads, without incident.  Going to bed now.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever3000 (edited 10-14-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000003||JohnF||10-14-2001||05:30 PM||||Jeff Blowers came by my house to pick parts off my '85 for a trial run before he had to buy new ones.  Sorry he couldn't get to the get together with us.<P>Next month is a get together at Loyde's, I think.  A "how to" for these little cars.   Keep us informed to when.||||reg||1
