Z||000012||FastFieros||10-15-2001||08:56 AM||||OK, I will help on the event and names.<P>From Left to right......<BR>Steve Wagner (IwannaIRM-88 Formula), Joe Meadows(88 GT-his car is at Ed Parks getting a 3.4), Pat Wilson (84 that is all show with 87 body and Ttops), Loyde Rascoe ( <A HREF="http://www.fastfieros.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fastfieros.com</A>  ), Steve Reid (84 3800SC with Ttops) John Fussel (JohnF-88 coupe nice all orginial), Ed Cheever (Cheever3000-88 GT) Mike Geddie(Humm needed a Fiero at this meet, but has a 86 SE), Jacob Elsworth (JetroGT-87 GT blue), Bryan Cheever (88 coupe not present at this meet, rode with dad.)<P>Ladies attending: Joe Meadows wife Diane, my Fiancee Yu Hui (english name EVA)<P>Dinner was Mexican food at some local dinner in Southlake.<P>Best topic of conversation: Fieros of course.<P>North Texas Fiero club regular meeting is Oct 27th at Papa's BBQ on Northwest Highway.<P>There is a lunch meeting at:<BR>October 20 Picnic at Huntsville state park. Reservations are Oct 20, the group shelter reserved from 8am to 9pm. It costs $3 per person to get into the park and $1-$2 each depending on how many show up to pay for the shelter. The shelter will hold 75 people so we have plenty of room. Please see <A HREF="http://www.flash.net/~newboy/lonestar.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.flash.net/~newboy/lonestar.html</A>  for details.<P>Hope to see everyone on the 27th in Dallas!<P>Loyde Rascoe <A HREF="http://www.fastfieros.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fastfieros.com</A> ||||reg||14
Z||000013||JSocha||10-15-2001||09:25 AM||||Hey guys!  Glad you all had a good time!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Wish I could have been there during this event!<P>Loki, you're such a goober!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  And thanks for sending me your phone number.<P>Loyde, that 86GT made it back to North Dakota.  Cylidner compression was 135-140/145.  The leak you spotted, was a round seal located on the timing gear housing, not the main gasket around the timing gear housing.  Timing chain was really, really stretched though.  Running like a top!  Working a little on it each weekend.  Thanks again, and it was nice meeting you when I was down in Dallas.<P>JohnF, you lucky devil!  Did you get that new Fiero home yet?<P>Cheev, you probably got my phone message after you got back.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Hope you had fun!?<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000014||JohnF||10-15-2001||09:28 AM||||Loyde - thanks "get-together" for the update.  <P>BTW - I think the Huntsville State Park Fiero show sponsors knew what they were doing.  This coming weekend (Oct. 20 - 21) is the ONLY time Texas State Park board offers FREE admission!<P>I hope I can be there (I hope, I hope, I hope!)  ||||reg||12
